\viewkind4\uc1\pard\cf1\ul\b\f0\fs24\'b6 Verse 1\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 1. Lord, Thy ransomed Church is waking
\par Out of slumber far and near,
\par Knowing that the morn is breaking
\par When the Bridegroom shall appear;
\par Waking up to claim the treasure
\par With Thy precious life-blood bought,
\par And to trust in fuller measure
\par All Thy wondrous death hath wrought.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 2\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 2. Praise to Thee for this glad shower,
\par Precious drops of latter rain;
\par Praise, that by Thy Spirit's power
\par Thou hast quickened us again;
\par That Thy gospel's priceless treasure
\par Now is borne from land to land,
\par And that all the Father's pleasure
\par Prospers in Thy pierced hand.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 3\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 3. Praise to Thee for saved ones yearning 
\par O'er the lost and wandering throng;
\par Praise for voices daily learning
\par To upraise the glad new song;
\par Praise to Thee for sick ones hasting
\par Now to touch Thy garment's hem;
\par Praise for souls believing, tasting
\par All Thy love has won for them.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 4\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 4. Set on fire our heart's devotion
\par With the love of Thy dear name;
\par Till o'er every land and ocean
\par Lips and lives Thy Cross proclaim;
\par Fix our eyes on Thy returning,
\par Keeping watch till Thou shalt come,
\par Lions well girt, lamps brightly burning;
\par Then, Lord, take Thy servants home. Amen.\f1 
\par \cf1\ul\b\fs16 
\par }

